    "abstract": "The paper studies model scaling and proposes compound scaling, which uniformly scales network depth, width, and resolution with a single coefficient phi. Using neural architecture search to obtain a baseline (EfficientNet-B0) and scaling it up yields EfficientNet-B1 to B7. EfficientNet-B7 achieves 84.3% ImageNet top-1 while being 8.4x smaller and 6.1x faster on inference than the best existing ConvNet, and the models transfer well.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Balancing depth, width, and resolution scaling is critical; scaling a single dimension saturates quickly.",
      "Compound scaling d = alpha^phi, w = beta^phi, r = gamma^phi with alpha * beta^2 * gamma^2 ≈ 2 scales FLOPs by about 2^phi.",
      "EfficientNet-B7 reaches 84.3% ImageNet top-1 with 66M parameters, 8.4x smaller and 6.1x faster than GPipe.",
      "EfficientNet-B0 reaches 77.1% top-1 with 5.3M parameters and 0.39B FLOPs.",
      "EfficientNets transfer well, achieving state-of-the-art accuracy on 5 of 8 transfer datasets with fewer parameters."
    ],
